437: ## 🆕 D12: Parada — Intermediate Stop Event Design
438: 
439: > **Status:** Design agreed, ready for Level 1 implementation (2026-04-07)
440: > **Renamed:** Originally "Retiro OC" → renamed to "Parada" because stops aren't always OC pickups.
441: > **Context:** Real example: SM-041 (MOV-2026-009). Trip went Taller → TUBOTEC → FEINSA → Muelle 14 → Taller. System only captured Salida/Entrega/Retorno — lost all supplier stop data.
442: 
443: ### The problem
444: Trips frequently make intermediate stops that the system can't record. These stops include:
445: - Retiro de OC en proveedor (most common — pickup purchase order materials)
446: - Entrega de tanques vacíos / material a devolver
447: - Buscar material en taller externo
448: - Dejar materiales en bodega/almacén de la empresa
449: - Intercambio (dejar y recoger en el mismo punto)
450: 
451: All share the same structure: conductor stops at a location, does something, optionally documents what happened.
452: 
453: ### Real-world flow (from Charris)
454: 1. Charris programs trip with lines from different origins (order of lines = route order)
455: 2. Conductor leaves Taller → goes to Supplier A → Supplier B → Project → returns to Taller
456: 3. At each stop: picks up/drops off material, sometimes receives invoice
457: 4. Conductor delivers everything to project
458: 5. For OC stops: project scans paper invoice, sends to Calderon (often weeks late)
459: 
460: ### What MovimientOS should capture
461: New event type: **"Parada"** — registered by conductor at each intermediate stop.
462: 
463: ```
464: MOV-2026-009 Timeline:
465:   🚛 Despacho    8:30  — Charris (Taller Chilibre)
466:   📍 Parada      9:15  — Conductor en TUBOTEC SA
467:        Tipo: Retiro de material
468:        OC 29902: PARCIAL — "Faltan 65 tubos PVC, los tendrán el jueves"
469:        📎 Factura-TUBOTEC-1234.pdf
470:   📍 Parada     10:30  — Conductor en FEINSA SA
471:        Tipo: Retiro de material
472:        OC 29903: COMPLETO
473:        📎 Factura-FEINSA-5678.pdf
474:   ✅ Entrega     1:45  — Jacome en Muelle 14
475:        Todo lo recogido entregado OK
476:   🏠 Retorno     3:35  — Conductor (Taller)
477: ```
478: 
479: ### Design decisions (confirmed with James 2026-04-07)
480: - **Name: "Parada"** — generic, covers all intermediate stop types
481: - Route is implicit from line order (no trip_stops table needed)
482: - OC works at bulk level (1 OC = 1 line), not item-by-item per Charris's preference
483: - Partial pickup is common — conductor always picks up what's available, notes what's pending
484: - Each supplier gives a separate invoice
485: - Parada is **informational** — does NOT change solicitud line status. Entrega at project is what changes status.
486: - Pending items from partial pickups are recorded as text notes (Level 1). Future levels add structured tracking.
487: - Calderon does NOT use the app. Invoice reach him via email notification with attachment link.
488: - The Parada button appears in the event buttons panel (mis-viajes/[id]) alongside Salida/Entrega/Retorno
489: - Lines from locations ≠ Taller Chilibre are auto-identified as potential intermediate stops
490: - Parada is optional — not required before Entrega. Available after Salida, before Retorno.
491: - Multiple Paradas per trip (one per stop)
492: 
